3,29],[34016,16.8,2017,55,105,26],[34312,16.9,1961,57,102,25],[34313,16.6,1961,51,100,28],[34612,16.9,1958,59,100,26]],"links":[["Ward County in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/north-dakota/ward-county"],["ARC or PLC in Ward County","/arc-plc/north-dakota/ward-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Ward County runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 17 grids September to October and October to November each came in under 90% of normal in 41 of 75 years. In 2025, on the county&rsquo;s middle value, October to November hit 189% of normal while February to March sat at 41%. So far in 2026, March to April and April to May each came in at 44% on the middle of the grids. Grid 33417 had its driest year in 1988 at 54%.</p>"}
